# Frontend Rules

- Use the existing React, TypeScript, and Vite setup.
- Inspect the existing components and routing before creating new ones.
- Follow the Gebeta UI design system.
- Build responsive layouts for mobile and desktop.
- Reuse existing UI components.
- Keep business logic out of presentation components.
- Use typed API response models.
- Do not invent backend endpoints.
- Implement loading, empty, error, and success states.
- Ensure all visible buttons and links perform real actions.
- Clearly label mock data and demo integrations.
- Do not expose service-role keys or AI credentials.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Avoid large rewrites when a focused change is sufficient.
